-- target: branch
--
-- W1-PROV — the 237 TAXONOMY NODES the rehearsal branch did not have.
--
-- Same class as `w1_prov_branch_registry_levelling.sql` and the same reason: §3 rule 36
-- levels the branch's SCHEMA with production, not its registry ROWS, and
-- `platform.taxonomy_node` is a registry the provisioner READS —
-- `registration.taxonomy_node_id` is a required spec field and the validator refuses any id
-- the table does not hold. Production carries 237 rows; the branch carried **zero**, so no
-- spec could name a legal node and nothing could be provisioned on the rehearsal branch at
-- all.
--
-- Every row is production's own, read SELECT-only 2026-09-17 and written verbatim, ordered
-- parent-before-child because `taxonomy_node_parent_id_fkey` is `ON DELETE RESTRICT` and
-- not deferrable. `created_by` and `updated_by` are NULL on all 237 rows on production, so
-- nothing here reaches `auth.users`; the single `organization_id` is the system
-- organization, which the branch already holds.
--
-- BRANCH ONLY, and it needs no production half: production already holds every row.
-- THE INVERSE: `migrations/inverse/w1_prov_branch_taxonomy_levelling_down.sql`.

set lock_timeout = '5s';
set statement_timeout = '300s';


